Lazy Evaluation

Consider:

numbers.stream()
       .filter(n -> n > 20)
       .map(n -> n * 2);

Nothing necessarily happens yet.

Why?

Because:

filter -> intermediate
map    -> intermediate

We haven't told Java to finish the pipeline.

Then:

.forEach(System.out::println);

is added.

Now processing occurs.

This is called lazy evaluation.